WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.249
Numbers, Time, Dates and Money.

2
00:00:02.529 --> 00:00:06.198
Day 11 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.948 --> 00:00:08.972
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.252 --> 00:00:15.673
Today's goal: say and understand prices, phone numbers, times, dates and spellings without confusion.

5
00:00:15.953 --> 00:00:19.836
You need these at every counter, on every call, and at every station.

6
00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:22.039
Part 1.

7
00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:23.301
Big numbers.

8
00:00:24.551 --> 00:00:25.895
Here is a quick table:

9
00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:27.433
Number, and Say it.

10
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:30.167
150: one hundred and fifty.

11
00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:34.265
1,250: one thousand two hundred and fifty.

12
00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:36.764
15,000: fifteen thousand.

13
00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:43.721
1,00,000 (Indian) = 100,000: one lakh = one hundred thousand.

14
00:00:44.001 --> 00:00:49.015
10,00,000 = 1,000,000: ten lakh = one million.

15
00:00:49.295 --> 00:00:54.820
1,00,00,000 = 10,000,000: one crore = ten million.

16
00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:56.810
Tip:

17
00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.949
With international colleagues, convert lakh and crore.

18
00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:07.034
25 lakh rupees, then about 2.5 million rupees or around 30,000 US dollars.

19
00:01:08.384 --> 00:01:18.389
Teens versus tens: say them clearly. thirTEEN (13) versus THIRty (30), fifTEEN (15) versus FIFty (50).

20
00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:19.992
If unsure, confirm:

21
00:01:20.272 --> 00:01:21.893
One-five or five-zero?

22
00:01:23.243 --> 00:01:24.118
Part 2.

23
00:01:24.398 --> 00:01:25.059
Money.

24
00:01:26.309 --> 00:01:29.723
250 rupees, then two hundred and fifty rupees.

25
00:01:30.003 --> 00:01:40.627
99.50 rupees, then ninety-nine rupees fifty (paise). $4.99, then four ninety-nine or four dollars ninety-nine cents.

26
00:01:40.907 --> 00:01:42.037
How much is it?

27
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:43.619
How much does it cost?

28
00:01:43.899 --> 00:01:44.944
What's the total?

29
00:01:45.224 --> 00:01:46.632
Is that including tax?

30
00:01:46.912 --> 00:01:49.045
That comes to 840 rupees.

31
00:01:49.325 --> 00:01:50.968
Here's 1,000 rupees.

32
00:01:51.248 --> 00:01:53.808
Your change is 160 rupees.

33
00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:56.054
Part 3.

34
00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:57.742
Phone numbers and codes.

35
00:01:58.992 --> 00:02:01.147
Say digits one by one, in groups:

36
00:02:01.427 --> 00:02:09.448
98450 12345, then nine-eight-four-five-oh, one-two-three-four-five.

37
00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:16.299
0 = zero or oh, 44 = double four, 777 = triple seven.

38
00:02:16.579 --> 00:02:18.115
Always read numbers back:

39
00:02:18.395 --> 00:02:20.464
Let me repeat that: nine-eight-four...

40
00:02:21.814 --> 00:02:22.731
Part 4.

41
00:02:23.011 --> 00:02:23.758
Time.

42
00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:26.352
Here is a quick table:

43
00:02:26.632 --> 00:02:27.805
Time, and Say it.

44
00:02:28.085 --> 00:02:30.475
7:00: seven o'clock.

45
00:02:30.755 --> 00:02:34.061
7:15: seven fifteen or quarter past seven.

46
00:02:34.341 --> 00:02:37.179
7:30: seven thirty or half past seven.

47
00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:41.043
7:45: seven forty-five or quarter to eight.

48
00:02:41.323 --> 00:02:44.011
7:10: seven ten or ten past seven.

49
00:02:44.291 --> 00:02:47.128
7:50: seven fifty or ten to eight.

50
00:02:47.408 --> 00:02:49.051
19:00:

51
00:02:49.331 --> 00:02:51.485
7 pm or seven in the evening.

52
00:02:52.835 --> 00:02:59.854
at 6 pm, in the morning or afternoon or evening, at night, around 7 (approximately), sharp (exactly:

53
00:03:00.134 --> 00:03:01.329
10 o'clock sharp).

54
00:03:02.679 --> 00:03:03.639
Part 5.

55
00:03:03.919 --> 00:03:04.708
Dates.

56
00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:06.705
Write:

57
00:03:06.985 --> 00:03:21.385
15 March 2026 or 15 or 03 or 2026 (India, UK), March 15, 2026 or 03 or 15 or 2026 (US).

58
00:03:21.665 --> 00:03:24.161
In global teams, write the month as a word.

59
00:03:24.441 --> 00:03:26.915
Say: the fifteenth of March or March fifteenth.

60
00:03:27.195 --> 00:03:28.049
Ordinals:

61
00:03:28.329 --> 00:03:45.331
1st first, 2nd second, 3rd third, 4th fourth, 5th fifth, 21st twenty-first, 22nd twenty-second, 31st thirty-first. on Monday or on 5 June, in June or in 2026, at the weekend (UK) / on the weekend (US).

62
00:03:46.681 --> 00:03:47.620
Part 6.

63
00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.137
Spelling out loud.

64
00:03:50.387 --> 00:03:52.990
Use a word for each letter when the line is bad:

65
00:03:53.270 --> 00:04:00.011
A for Apple, B for Bombay, S for Sugar, M for Mumbai, N for Nagpur, P for Pune, D for Delhi...

66
00:04:01.361 --> 00:04:02.300
You could say:

67
00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.903
My name is Gupta:

68
00:04:04.183 --> 00:04:08.705
G for Goa, U for Umbrella, P for Pune, T for Tiger, A for Apple.

69
00:04:10.055 --> 00:04:10.994
Part 7.

70
00:04:11.274 --> 00:04:13.813
Conversation: booking a table on the phone.

71
00:04:15.063 --> 00:04:17.089
Here is how the conversation goes.

72
00:04:17.369 --> 00:04:19.012
Good evening, Spice Garden.

73
00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.551
How can I help you?

74
00:04:20.831 --> 00:04:25.417
Hi, I'd like to book a table for six people on Saturday, the 14th.

75
00:04:25.697 --> 00:04:26.401
Sure.

76
00:04:26.681 --> 00:04:27.663
What time?

77
00:04:27.943 --> 00:04:29.607
At 8 pm, please.

78
00:04:29.887 --> 00:04:30.996
Let me check...

79
00:04:31.276 --> 00:04:32.705
Yes, that's available.

80
00:04:32.985 --> 00:04:34.287
Could I have your name?

81
00:04:35.637 --> 00:04:37.237
The conversation continues.

82
00:04:37.517 --> 00:04:38.306
Gupta.

83
00:04:38.586 --> 00:04:43.770
G for Goa, U for Umbrella, P for Pune, T for Tiger, A for Apple.

84
00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.159
Thank you.

85
00:04:45.439 --> 00:04:46.655
And a phone number?

86
00:04:46.935 --> 00:04:52.205
It's 98450 12345.

87
00:04:52.485 --> 00:04:56.666
98450 12345?

88
00:04:56.946 --> 00:04:57.970
That's right.

89
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.920
The conversation continues.

90
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.032
Done.

91
00:05:02.312 --> 00:05:05.512
A table for six, Saturday the 14th, at 8 pm.

92
00:05:05.792 --> 00:05:06.688
Perfect.

93
00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:09.229
Is there a minimum charge for groups?

94
00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.747
No, there isn't.

95
00:05:11.027 --> 00:05:12.285
Great, thank you.

96
00:05:12.565 --> 00:05:14.101
See you on Saturday!

97
00:05:15.451 --> 00:05:16.326
Part 8.

98
00:05:16.606 --> 00:05:17.523
Practice.

99
00:05:18.773 --> 00:05:19.413
1.

100
00:05:19.693 --> 00:05:20.909
Say these out loud:

101
00:05:21.189 --> 00:05:33.200
4,75,000 rupees, 9:45, 22nd August, 080 2345 6677, 1.5 crore.

102
00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:35.467
Success:

103
00:05:35.747 --> 00:05:50.531
Answers. four lakh seventy-five thousand rupees, nine forty-five or quarter to ten, the twenty-second of August, oh-eight-oh, two-three-four-five, six-six-seven-seven (double six, double seven), one and a half crore (fifteen million).

104
00:05:51.881 --> 00:05:52.585
2.

105
00:05:52.865 --> 00:05:54.081
Choose at, on or in:

106
00:05:54.361 --> 00:05:58.265
7 pm, Monday, July, the morning, 25 December.

107
00:05:59.615 --> 00:06:00.533
Success:

108
00:06:00.813 --> 00:06:02.669
Answers. at, on, in, in, on.

109
00:06:04.019 --> 00:06:04.765
3.

110
00:06:05.045 --> 00:06:09.675
Spell your full name using a word for each letter, then say your phone number in groups.

111
00:06:11.025 --> 00:06:11.921
Part 9.

112
00:06:12.201 --> 00:06:13.246
Speak today.

113
00:06:14.496 --> 00:06:17.483
Read back one phone number or amount to confirm it.

114
00:06:17.763 --> 00:06:20.301
Spell your name with the A for Apple method once.

115
00:06:20.581 --> 00:06:23.995
Ask Is that including tax? or What's the total? at a shop.

116
00:06:25.345 --> 00:06:26.881
That's the end of this lesson.

117
00:06:27.161 --> 00:06:31.811
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

118
00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:38.214
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

